<k>marrowfast</k>
<blockquote><blockquote><b>marrowfast</b></blockquote></blockquote>
<blockquote><blockquote>(<c c="darkslategray">ˈmærəʊfɑːst</c>)</blockquote></blockquote>
<blockquote><blockquote><c c="gray">[f. <i>marrow</i> n. + <i>fast</i> a.]</c></blockquote></blockquote>
<blockquote><blockquote><b><c c="indigo">1.</c></b> Firmly jointed; (of timber) close-grained.</blockquote></blockquote>
<blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><ex><b>1712</b> <i>J. Ward</i> <i>Carpentry</i> 19 <c c="darkmagenta">Oak well marrowfast.</c> <b>Ibid.</b> 24 <c c="darkmagenta">A marrowfast beam.</c></ex></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote>
<blockquote><blockquote><b><c c="indigo">2.</c></b> <i>fig.</i> Steadfast; loyal.</blockquote></blockquote>
<blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><ex><i>Poems of the North</i> 44 <c c="darkmagenta">Marrowfast in friendship.</c></ex></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote>
